 Just a few (crazy) suggestions:

 A new feature for a crystal ball:

 "You see futuristic visions. You turn into a Jedi !"

 If the ball is blessed, the permanency will be asked,
 if normal, the knighthood lasts in 400-600 turns,
 and if cursed, the ball zaps your mind...

 The Jedi is able to use telekinesis, so he/she could pick up stuff by using
 his/her will. Use of telekinesis decreases 'Pw' depending on the size
 of the object. Of course you're able to move your enemies out of your sight
 in case you have enough Pw. BUT ! If you have eg Pw 32 and your enemy has
 Pw 40 and you try to get rid of him/her by telekinesis, he/she confuses
 you and your Pw decreases (40-32=8) by 2*8, so, now you've got Pw 16(32).
 If the Pw decreases to negative, you die. ("Lobotomized by *****" or 
 something like that...). If the Pws are equal, "your head aches".


   The telekinesis is a Jedi instinct, but it's rumoured, that the ring of
 telekinesis has been hidden deep ... 

   The +2 ring of telekinesis doubles your Pw
       +3 ring of telekinesis triples your Pw and so on. 
         ( +3 rot; could be found once in a hundred years while full moon)
       -2 ring of telekinesis halves your Pw and so on.


   Telekinesis is a superb way to rob a shop: Just fly the objects out of
 the shop ! (Well, now I pile all the stuff together and use the wand of tele-
 portation...)

   It's also useful in fights: A room. One large box, 3 snakes and a nymph.
 You use your kinetic power and the box levitates to the 1st snake. The box
 lands on the snake. Squirt! The snake dies. Moving the box lowered Pw by one
 on every second move. But what about the nymph ? If I smashed her with the
 box, her mirror cracks to useless and my luck reduces... Hmmm. I'll fly her
 against the wall... Smash! She tries to smile... Another hmmm. What if I
 stole her mirror with telekinesis ...? Yeah! It works! (a leprechaun enters
 the room). Well, I need some money... 1268 gold pieces levitates to you...
 You feel exhausted (Pw has lowered to 5(32)). 

   And so on

   (But no laser weaponry while the idea was telekinesis...!) 


   Well, it sounds good to me, but is it useful ?
   Any comments ?


